4.—(1) For 2023, the amount of contribution to be paid under section 9(1)(b) of the Act is —
(a)$230 for a non-schooling member who is at least 7 years of age but below 13 years of age;
(b)$230 for a non-schooling member who —
(i)is at least 13 years of age but below 15 years of age;
(ii)is receiving home‑schooling in accordance with the terms and conditions in paragraph 3(2)(a) and (b)(i) and (ii) of the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order (O 1) and such other terms and conditions as the Minister thinks fit under that Order; and
(iii)did not perform, in 2022, at the Primary School Leaving Examination and the National Education Quiz, at such level of educational achievement as the Director‑General of Education may determine;
(c)$230 for a non-schooling member who —
(i)is at least 13 years of age but below 17 years of age;
(ii)does not attain 17 years of age at any time in 2023; and
(iii)is receiving primary education in a designated school; and
(d)$290 for a non-schooling member not mentioned in sub‑paragraph (b) or (c), who —
(i)is at least 13 years of age but below 17 years of age; and
(ii)does not attain 17 years of age at any time in 2023.
(2) In this paragraph —
“designated school”, “home‑schooling”, “National Education Quiz” and “Primary School Leaving Examination” have the meanings given by the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order;
“non-schooling member” means a member of the Edusave Pupils Fund who is not a full‑time student of a prescribed school at any time during 2023.
